                "entry_id": "17c0ae86-c3fa-30c6-9bc1-101cf0e6a9d7",
                "word": "validisme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "49f2dcfc-d03d-46c3-8532-393dcdd5fc08",
                        "entry_id": "17c0ae86-c3fa-30c6-9bc1-101cf0e6a9d7",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "validismes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "37b136f8-3286-3b22-a75c-d1f9fb04e91a",
                        "entry_id": "17c0ae86-c3fa-30c6-9bc1-101cf0e6a9d7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Oppression vécue par les personnes en situation de handicap physique ou mental."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Handicap",
                            "Luttes sociales"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2c42b7c-6b93-4272-ba28-64466898e888",
                                "sense_id": "37b136f8-3286-3b22-a75c-d1f9fb04e91a",
                                "text": "Nous devons contester le validisme sous toutes ses formes, et nous interroger sur cette sagesse qui consiste à s’adapter à une société oppressive et malsaine, une société qui à bien des égards, est elle-même assez folle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2baf7cd2-955a-4973-80e3-8b11030f458f",
                                "sense_id": "37b136f8-3286-3b22-a75c-d1f9fb04e91a",
                                "text": "Le validisme, la norme du/de la valide, régit le fonctionnement de tout le monde."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "26e9d8f1-e630-4835-94c9-ef1f36ff9881",
                        "source_entry_id": "17c0ae86-c3fa-30c6-9bc1-101cf0e6a9d7",
                        "source_sense_id": "37b136f8-3286-3b22-a75c-d1f9fb04e91a",
                        "target_lang_word": "ableism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ableism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "19540ff0-4083-34a7-b162-0a3c066fd082",
                                        "entry_id": "02cadc24-8648-35e8-a926-9383552b1a34",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Discrimination against people with disabilities in favor of those without."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da498c97-9060-45f3-b244-f30256608b1a",
                                                "sense_id": "19540ff0-4083-34a7-b162-0a3c066fd082",
                                                "text": "Ableism is your ability to find reasons to push us aside to keeps us in cages, leave our struggles out of the history pages … pretend we never existed. Ableism is when you say I'm the only disabled friend you've ever had. Ableism is when you say that and still don't understand why we feel invisible. Ableism is when you think I don't have a disability because you can't see it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c44bd5d-47fc-325a-a796-d412debb881a",
                                        "entry_id": "02cadc24-8648-35e8-a926-9383552b1a34",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An instance of ableism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53a313c2-7d32-4376-81ed-0cab7dd92fba",
                                                "sense_id": "1c44bd5d-47fc-325a-a796-d412debb881a",
                                                "text": "Developing guidelines around which ableisms and favoritisms of abilities are ethical , e.g. which form and shape of competitiveness might be ethical and which might not, can be a useful tool for the governance of S&T."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f5c12c5-beff-4bb9-9d86-76219239be88",
                                                "sense_id": "1c44bd5d-47fc-325a-a796-d412debb881a",
                                                "text": "And, as a media and communication PhD, I know this is because the English language itself is a media so biased, with ableisms so deeply built in, that roads (which seem to lead away from ableisms) in fact, lead directly back into them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e38f175a-1fd2-4a7c-878a-88dd4636b641",
                                                "sense_id": "1c44bd5d-47fc-325a-a796-d412debb881a",
                                                "text": "Ultimately, NTWH mobilieze Stanislavsky not despite the ableisms that Sandahl identifies but on the basis that a critical rehabilitation of those ableisms might create the very conditions of authenticity in which people with disabilities could enter both the theatrical workforce and the braoader affective labor market."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
